{"id": "EUVD-2026-76503", "enisaUuid": "b12ef69f-59b2-3568-940f-834092af7953", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naccel/rocket: initialize job domain before cleanup paths\n\nrocket_ioctl_submit_job() releases rjob through rocket_job_put() on\nallocation error paths. rocket_job_cleanup() unconditionally calls\nrocket_iommu_domain_put(job->domain), but job->domain is assigned only\nafter task copying and BO lookups. A failure before that assignment can\ntherefore clean up a job with a NULL domain pointer.\n\nTake the per-file domain reference before the first error path can release\nrjob. Also clear rjob->tasks after freeing it in rocket_copy_tasks(), so\nthe common cleanup path cannot free the task array again after a task-copy\nerror.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3043230296653a609ab50006899e64bbb2d99465", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/81731f1eda5e6a1dfad31445f741de9bbefbb08e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/70e6a33d68a9b03335c5426332666e52d07f45d6"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pp5j-w2pr-xvv3", "CVE-2026-89591"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0fcfae04-e75d-3439-911d-84f82c615aae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "393be32e-a204-3aad-8d44-5bf26a82f376", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5d9ce8ef-4366-3940-bfa7-094f922625b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0810d5ad88a18f1e6d549853a388ad0316f74e36 <70e6a33d68a9b03335c5426332666e52d07f45d6"}, {"id": "888d077f-4b44-349e-8be3-f90e1d077cc1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0810d5ad88a18f1e6d549853a388ad0316f74e36 <3043230296653a609ab50006899e64bbb2d99465"}, {"id": "948bfad3-dff0-3d21-88cb-fd0237a87cb0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "a6d88258-c2cc-3af8-8d31-efcf8296dcba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0810d5ad88a18f1e6d549853a388ad0316f74e36 <81731f1eda5e6a1dfad31445f741de9bbefbb08e"}, {"id": "efb2cec8-787c-394a-af0c-581c9b9eddfe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "f6d14657-9d39-32e1-a06c-a9745bdbd7b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "039f20f5-b81d-3a82-9afb-7fb2a6e095c4", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}